{"name":"Bubble Shell","hex":"#d3a49a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bubble shell","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the headshield slugs of genus Bulla, belonging to the order Cephalaspidea of gastropods.\n A marine univalve shell of the genus Bulla (Bullidae) and certain shells of similar appearance of the now disused order Tectibranchiata of molluscs.","A marine univalve shell of the genus Bulla (Bullidae) and certain shells of similar appearance of the now disused order Tectibranchiata of molluscs."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bubble_shell"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cephalaspidea","blocks":[{"text":"The order Cephalaspidea, also known as the  headshield slugs and bubble snails, is a major taxon of sea slugs and bubble snails, marine gastropod mollusks within the larger clade Euopisthobranchia. Bubble shells is another common name for these families of marine gastropods, some of which have thin bubble-like shells. This clade contains more than 600 species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Chelidonura_varians.jpg/330px-Chelidonura_varians.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cephalaspidea","wikidata":"Q1371035"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Bulla_ampulla_01.JPG/250px-Bulla_ampulla_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Bulla_ampulla_01.JPG/500px-Bulla_ampulla_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Bulla_ampulla_01.JPG/250px-Bulla_ampulla_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABulla_ampulla_01.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/common